# Beats against the REAL server with the simulator alone: two Talk turns from a list of clips, and the
# offline beat shown with the simulator's own network switch (o), no server pause needed.
# Run: walker simulate --server <url> --state <dir> --mic-file ask.wav,front.wav --script test/sim/real-server-beats.walk

expect spoke Sophi is on.
expect link online
expect heartbeat ok

# Turn 1 (first clip). Without a model key the server answers with a fixed line, marked as such.
key t
expect talk recording
expect mic open
wait 1200
key t
expect turn answered

# Offline with the switch: down, the walker says so; a Talk press gets the same line (sent to the page once).
key o
expect 30000 link offline
expect spoke I'm offline right now.
key t
expect spoke I'm offline right now.
absent 1000 talk recording

# Back up: the walker says so, and turn 2 uses the second clip.
key o
expect 30000 link online
expect spoke I'm back online.
key t
expect talk recording
expect mic open
wait 1200
key t
expect turn answered
key q
